          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "પૂર્વ — pūrva — \"the east\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "સૂરજ પૂર્વમાં ઊગે છે. sūraj pūrvamā̃ ūge che. The sun rises in the east."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A feminine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "પૂર્વ (pūrva) is a tatsama, Sanskrit pūrva, \"in front, before\", and so \"eastern\" (Monier-Williams): facing the sunrise, the east is in front of you."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
